# Line-ending policy.
#
# This exists because of a real failure, not as boilerplate. `models/scorer.txt` is a
# LightGBM model dump: text to git, but a strict format to LightGBM. With git's default
# autocrlf on Windows it was checked out with CRLF endings, and a fresh clone died with
#
#     [LightGBM] [Fatal] Model format error, expect a tree here.
#
# on every prediction. The repo worked perfectly for the author and was broken for
# everyone who cloned it. Caught by SPEC 8.4's clone test; it would otherwise have been
# found by a judge.

# Source and docs: LF in the repo, normalised on commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Artefacts that must survive byte-for-byte. `binary` implies -text -diff.
models/scorer.txt binary
models/metrics.json -text

# Committed agent decisions. The reproducibility claim in SPEC 4.3 is byte-for-byte
# replay, so these must not be rewritten on checkout either.
cache/llm/*.json -text

# Generated data is gitignored, but pin it in case that ever changes.
data/*.csv -text
data/*.jsonl -text
